 ## Background
-The RawNeRF variant of the photometric loss was introduced to address bias in inverse rendering models that use cache-based predictions [S2]. It builds on the standard NeRF photometric loss [S1] and applies the gradient trick [10] to ensure correct gradient propagation through Monte Carlo estimators. The method is used in physically-based inverse rendering frameworks to supervise NeRF caches against physically-based models [S2].
+The RawNeRF variant of the photometric loss was introduced to address bias in inverse rendering models that use cache-based predictions [S3]. It builds on the standard NeRF photometric loss [S1] and applies the gradient trick [S3] to ensure correct gradient propagation through Monte Carlo estimators. The method is used in physically-based inverse rendering frameworks to supervise NeRF caches against physically-based models [S3].
 
